  "about": "Split suggestions from agent activity. The Mac's Kit (SplitSuggestionVectorTests.swift) and the API (SplitSuggestionVectorTests.cs) both run these cases, so a split suggested on the web is the one the Mac suggests. Times are wall-clock times in timeZone. A session without a repository ran in a folder outside git. Projects are referred to by key; the entry's project is the time the logs leave open. Each part's prompts are those sent within the entry, and strength says how loudly the suggestion may be offered. A session's branches are those it ran on; rules are branch rules on a repository's link, in order, and a part's task is the one its rule names. branchPatterns are how a rule's pattern reads a branch.",
